(a) Information and instructions regarding the peculiarities of normal operations (including starting and warming the engines, taxiing, operation of wing flaps, landing gear, and the automatic pilot) must be furnished, together with recommended procedures for--
  (1) Engine failure (including minimum speeds, trim, operation of the remaining engines, and operation of flaps);
  (2) Stopping the rotation of propellers in flight;
  (3) Restarting turbine engines in flight (including the effects of altitude);
  (4) Fire, decompression, and similar emergencies;
  (5) Ditching (including the procedures based on the requirements of Secs. 25.801, 25.807(d), 25.1411, and 25.1415 (a) through (e)); and
  (6) Use of ice protection equipment.

